  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Late-inning rallies keep finding their moment. This one arrived in the ninth.",
    "what_this_means": "Fermin powered the early offense with a three-run night that kept the Padres relevant through six innings, but the game turned in the eighth when the Giants went ahead. That's when the margin disappeared entirely. Cronenworth's single in the ninth recaptured a lead the Padres had already held in the second and fourth innings, turning a night of momentum swings. Lead changes in the first, third, fourth, and eighth. Into a two-run win. The offense scratched out six runs on ten hits without ever dominating a moment; they converted two of seven RISP situations and made those runs count. Wandy Peralta and Adrian Morejon shut the door across 2.2 innings before the bats answered late. This is a team that doesn't need clean innings. Just the last one. Three straight one-run wins. That math gets harder.",
